    "Synthetic seller corpus and synthetic customer questions. No real seller or customer text.",
    "requiredKnowledge: titles the retrieval must reach. sellerInputRequired: the honest answer is that the",
    "company has not written this down — the draft must refuse and the gap must name expectedMissingSubject.",
    "mustSupport: a figure or word the answer may only carry because the corpus states it.",
    "mustNotClaim: sentences that would be false or unauthorised on this corpus.",
    "2026-09-18 first measurement corrected four labels: Q26 names the Answer Memory entry's own title, and Q33 is grounded (the corpus does mention 밝기 단계) with the invented count as mustNotClaim. Q20·Q21·Q22 keep sellerInputRequired=true and are the measured false-grounding cases."
